          "topic": "Arithmetic progressions",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "An arithmetic progression (AP) is a sequence with a constant difference d between consecutive terms. Its nth term is a_n = a + (n - 1)d. The sum of the first n terms is S_n = n/2[2a + (n - 1)d], or n/2(a + l) when the last term l is known.",
